# Flyway — partitioned tables (audit log, auth attempts)

Apply when writing Flyway migrations or entities that reference `ezkey_audit_log` or
`ezkey_auth_attempt`.

## Greenfield mindset (pre-production)

Write migrations as if designing the final schema **now**, not as a minimal fix for an earlier
omission. Ezkey has no production database; prefer the natural PostgreSQL formulation.

## Composite identity

| Table | Partitioning | FK / PK shape (if ever needed) |
|-------|--------------|--------------------------------|
| `ezkey_auth_attempt` | RANGE (`created_at`) | `(auth_attempt_id, created_at)` — PK in V4 |
| `ezkey_audit_log` | RANGE + LIST (`api_name`) | `(audit_log_id, created_at, api_name)` — **no parent PK today** |

Unique constraints on partitioned parents **must include every partition key column**. Audit log
is **not** the same shape as auth attempt; `PRIMARY KEY (audit_log_id, created_at)` fails
(`SQLSTATE 0A000`, missing `api_name`).

## Referencing audit entries

| Need | Pattern |
|------|---------|
| Row lives only while audit entry exists | Composite FK including `api_name` if targeting `ezkey_audit_log` |
| Durable overlay must survive audit **purge** | Snapshot `(audit_log_id, audit_log_created_at)` **without FK** (e.g. entry integrity conciliation) |

## Audit log is purgeable

Archive lifecycle (`SEAL → [EXPORTED] → PURGEABLE → physical delete`) removes audit rows from
sealed partitions. Do **not** assume audit entries are permanent. Restrictive FKs block purge;
`ON DELETE CASCADE` destroys operator narrative.

## Invalid pattern (fails at migrate time)

```sql
-- WRONG: audit_log_id alone has no unique constraint on partitioned parent
FOREIGN KEY (audit_log_id) REFERENCES ezkey_audit_log (audit_log_id)
```

